---
source: crates/dyno-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: "help(&[\"receipt\", \"sign\", \"--help\"])"
---
[phase 3] Sign a receipt for a result file from `dyno check` with a run on a device

Usage: dyno receipt sign [OPTIONS] --key <FILE> --result <FILE> --issuer <NAME> --check-id <ID>

Options:
      --key <FILE>          [phase 3] The private key file that `dyno receipt keygen` wrote
      --result <FILE>       [phase 3] The result file from `dyno check` to sign a receipt for
      --issuer <NAME>       [phase 3] The lab's name, such as its domain
      --check-id <ID>       [phase 3] The lab's id for the run
      --lab-kind <KIND>     [phase 3] What kind of lab it is, in the lab's own words [default: own_phones]
      --lab-backend <NAME>  [phase 3] What the lab's devices run on, such as the name of a device cloud
      --issued-at <TIME>    [phase 3] When the lab signs, in UTC to the second, such as 2026-11-25T10:00:00Z [default: now]
      --out <FILE>          [phase 3] Write the receipt to FILE, which must not be there yet, instead of stdout
  -h, --help                Print help

Exit codes:
  0   the receipt is signed
  64  usage or input error: a private key file that cannot be read or is not one, or a result
      that cannot be read, was edited, or has no build or no device
  70  internal or I/O error, such as a receipt file that cannot be written
